TI  - fetuin-a as a marker of insulin resistance
PY  - 2023
T2  - Experimental and Applied Biomedical Research (EABR)
VL  - 24
IS  - 4
SP  - 289
EP  - 295
DO  - 10.2478/sjecr-2021-0042
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85183104280&doi=10.2478%2fsjecr-2021-0042&partnerID=40&md5=fca4c15f5de899138022efcbfa98397f
AB  - Fetuin-a is a glycoprotein which helps in the regulation of metab¬olism. It is an early marker of insulin resistance (ir). The aim of this study ttm to evaluate the role of fetuin-a as a predictive bi- omarker in cases of newly delected type 2 diabetes (\'dd). The study involved 60 ndd and 60 normal healthy controls (nhc). All the demographics and anthropological characteristics were noted. Fasting blood samples here drawn and various biochemi¬cal parameters were analyzed. The homeostatic model assess¬ment of insulin resistance (homa-ir) and the quantitative insulin sensitivity check index (quick!) Score was calculated. Chi- square. Student t-test and mann whitney v tests were employed to associate and compare the mean and median between the ndd and nhc groups. Pearson's and spearman's correlation analysis were employed to examine the relationship of fetuin-a levels with parametric and nonparametric variables. The independent pre¬dictors of fetuin-a was determined by employing multiple for¬ward linear regression. Fetuin-a was significantly high in ndd compared to nhc (1323 vs. 306.98 mcg/ml; p<0.001). Majority of ndd patients demonstrated 1r based on the homa-ir (88.33% vs. 66.67%) and quick! Score (96.67% vs. 85%). The multiple linear regression analysis showed that systolic blood pressure, age and quick1 score were independently associated with fetuin-a (p value <0.01). Fetuin-a may be used as a bi- omarker to delect ndd. Therefore, early detection of fetuin-a levels in ndd gives an opportunity for suitable patient manage¬ment. © 2023 The Author(s).
