UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85174982124&doi=10.1201%2f9781003386308-10&partnerID=40&md5=6cf0cb466308fb8d22209a9e03ce8cb7
AB  - Diabetes mellitus is one of the prevailing metabolic disorders affecting globally. The current data says around 422 million people are affected with diabetes globally and this fact of global spreading is very well understood by the recognized institutions such as WHO, USDA, IDF, and CDA. Prediabetes, type 1, type 2, gestational diabetes, and other specific etiologic types are a few important classes of diabetes with urbanization, lifestyle, and genetic susceptibility as the main cause. Diet and supplements had a great role in prevention as well as management of diabetes, even the long-term complications of diabetes can be prevented or delayed. The common dietary supplements recommended in diabetes are micronutrients, antioxidants, dietary fibers, vitamins, and phyto foods. The details of all these dietary materials beneficial in diabetes along with examples, source, role, mechanism, and other recent research are explained in the chapter. © 2024 Apple Academic Press, Inc. Co-published with CRC Press (Taylor & Francis). All rights reserved.
