TI  - Molecular Processes Involved in the Shared Pathways between Cardiovascular Diseases and Diabetes
PY  - 2023
T2  - Biomedicines
VL  - 11
IS  - 10
C7  - 2611
DO  - 10.3390/biomedicines11102611
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85175177962&doi=10.3390%2fbiomedicines11102611&partnerID=40&md5=cf432a26a90661c6469d2816fe13f4d9
AB  - Cardiovascular diseases and diabetes mellitus are currently among the diseases with the highest morbidity and mortality. The pathogenesis and development of these diseases remain strongly connected, along with inflammation playing a major role. Therefore, the treatment possibilities showing a positive impact on both of these diseases could be especially beneficial for patients. SGLT-2 inhibitors and GLP-1 receptor agonists present this dual effect. Moreover, the hostile composition of the gut microbiota could influence the progression of these conditions. In this review, the authors present the latest knowledge on and innovations in diabetes mellitus and CVD—with the focus on the molecular mechanisms and the role of the microbiota. © 2023 by the authors.
