TI  - Hepatic metabolism-related effects of polysaccharides from red kidney bean and small black soybean on type 2 diabetes
PY  - 2023
T2  - Food Chemistry
VL  - 403
C7  - 134334
DO  - 10.1016/j.foodchem.2022.134334
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85138480934&doi=10.1016%2fj.foodchem.2022.134334&partnerID=40&md5=aefe4cdacdcc340b1ee888a4e2ed9845
AB  - In our previous study, two crude polysaccharides from red kidney bean and small black soybean (RK, SB) have shown the alleviative effect on type 2 diabetic mice. Meanwhile, hepatic dysfunction usually accompanied with type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM), and closely related to glucose and lipid homeostasis. Therefore, this time we further investigated the protective effect on hepatic dysfunction of RK and SB. Results found that both crude polysaccharides had the protective effects. In addition, investigation on purified polysaccharides identified that the polysaccharide was the biofunctional component basis in crude RK and SB. Subsequently, further research investigated the regulating mechanism of two pure polysaccharides (RKPH and SBPH) on hepatic metabolism and lipid metabolism. The results showed the improved different metabolites of phosphatidylcholine (PC) and phosphatidylethanolamine (PE) by RKPH and SBPH to affect glycerophospholipid metabolism pathway might be involved in the improvement of the glucose, lipids homeostasis and liver function in T2DM. © 2022
