AB  - Diabetes is a chronic metabolic syndrome that affects millions of people throughout the world. The Improper selection of drugs and their doses and undesirable side effects pose the problem in the treatment of diabetes. Due to few side effects and the high efficiency of new drugs, there is increasing interest in searching for herbal sources. However, formulation of several plant-derived compounds and their drug delivery systems was found to be slow due to the complexity of active compounds. In this respect, varied nanoformulations have been developed for herbal drugs and found equally efficient to chemically nanoparticle formulations in the treatment of diabetes. This chapter summarizes the current knowledge on various plant-derived drugs, potentization using sanjeevan system, and nanoformulations for control of diabetes and related complications. © 2024 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
