AB  - Gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) has emerged as a disorder that can raise women’s and their offspring’s future health concerns. Limited drug use during pregnancy causes people to turn to natural substances for the prevention of diabetes mellitus during pregnancy. The bioactive substance that gives chili peppers their bitter flavor, capsaicin, is derived from the Gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) has emerged as a disorder that can raise women’s and their offspring’s future health concerns. Limited drug use during pregnancy causes people to turn to natural substances for the prevention of diabetes mellitus during pregnancy. The bioactive substance that gives chili peppers their bitter flavor, capsaicin, is derived from the Capsicum plant. Capsaicin has recently been utilized to treat a variety of illnesses, including obesity, type 2 diabetes, insulin resistance, and fatty liver disease by controlling metabolic dysregulations such as hyperglycemia, hyperinsulinemia, and hyperlipidemia. This chapter aims to shed light on the effect of capsaicin administration on improving insulin sensitivity and treating lipid abnormalities in GDM-affected females, covering recent findings. © 2024 John Wiley & Sons, Inc.
