UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85170166703&doi=10.1201%2f9781003333821-10&partnerID=40&md5=f86ac4525b2aed29ff8fce4883056e06
AB  - The nutraceutical industry has a market cap of 111.9 billion USD in the United States and 454.6 billion USD globally in 2021 and is forecasted to grow 7.5% annually from 2021-2030. This chapter highlights evidence regarding the efficacy and effectiveness of some nutraceuticals used to manage anxiety and the gut microbiome. Popular nutraceuticals discussed include cannabidiol, B vitamins, magnesium, fatty acids, vitamin D, Melissa officinalis, prebiotics, probiotics, postbiotics, and synbiotics. We reviewed several systematic reviews, meta-analyses, randomized controlled trials etc., to appraise the evidence supporting these nutraceuticals. This chapter highlights that while these nutraceuticals have shown promise in improving anxiety and other conditions, further robust research is needed regarding the efficacy, dose, method of delivery, adverse events, and mechanism of action of many of the nutraceuticals. © 2024 Yashwant V. Pathak, Sarvadaman Pathak, and Con Stough.
