AB  - Machine learning system is used in this study to estimate the risk assessment of pregnancy. Many factor caused during pregnancy is a dangerous condition that affects pregnant women as well as fetuses. Gestational diabetes (GD), high BP, PCOS, thyroid illness, and other main conditions all increase the risk. For researchers, it is difficult to predict these disorders. The analysis in this paper was done to forecast the high risk in pregnancy using machine learning approaches. The LR, RF, SVM, and KNN algorithms were computed and compared with various settings. The datasets are obtained via Kaggle and DHS. Python was used to calculate the results. The result of random forest is better than the other models like linear regression, KNN, and SVM. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd.
