TI  - The role of inositols in maternal adaptation, placental function, and regulation of fetal growth and development
PY  - 2023
T2  - A Clinical Guide to Inositols
SP  - 87
EP  - 110
DO  - 10.1016/B978-0-323-91673-8.00013-3
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85167762474&doi=10.1016%2fB978-0-323-91673-8.00013-3&partnerID=40&md5=06bd1404c97d75725a06d07dbf86d661
AB  - The goal of pregnancy is to deliver a healthy baby. Optimal maternal adaptation to pregnancy and good maternal-placental-fetal communications play important roles in ensuring a good outcome. Inositol is expected to play a part in many of these important pregnancy events but they remain poorly understood. Inositol and its derivatives are involved in altering maternal tissue function to promote maternal adaptation, regulating placental function, and modulating fetal growth and development. In this chapter, we will summarize the current knowledge and, wherever possible, provide likely scenarios of inositol's involvement based on our understanding in related biological systems. © 2023 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
