AB  - Viral hepatitis is one of the more commonly diagnosed viral infections in pregnancy. Globally, it causes 1.34 million deaths per year. There are more than five subtypes of hepatitis that were being identified, namely Hepatitis A, B, C, D, and E. They have different routes of transmission with various impacts during pregnancy, which require individualized management during pregnancy. This chapter describes each type of hepatitis and its maternal, fetal, and perinatal implications. © 2023 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
