AB  - The concepts of personalized nutrition and health have been known for over 2 millennia but the molecular processes that vary between individuals are only now being subjected to the advanced technologies of the modern era. The initial studies of personalized responses to nutrition focused almost exclusively on gene—nutrient interactions. Essentially all omics tools are now being used to assess how nutrients influence epigenetic markers, transcripts, metabolites, proteins, and the microbiome and, conversely, how genetics and molecular processes alter nutrient metabolism. The knowledge base for personalized nutrition is being accelerated by adoption of n-of-1 study designs, complementing the more traditional cross-sectional case/control designs. © 2023 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
