VL  - 29
IS  - 5
SP  - 509
EP  - 514
DO  - 10.19526/j.cnki.1005-8915.20220514
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85143972184&doi=10.19526%2fj.cnki.1005-8915.20220514&partnerID=40&md5=1b3ed7dfd789da16f8fac2b366731de5
AB  - Circular RNA (circRNA), a class of endogenous non-coding RNA with covalently closed continuous loop structure, was revealed to be abundant in mammalian cells and characterized by highly conserved, tissue-specific, disease-specific and time-specific.With the wide application of molecular biology and high-throughput sequencing technology, the researchers' understanding of circRNA has been greatly enriched in recent years, and the important regulatory role of circRNA in the occurrence and development of diabetes has been also confirmed.Currently, the diagnosis and treatment of diabetes are mostly focused on blood glucose monitoring and management, and it is important to explore new diagnostic and therapeutic ideas.Furthermore, circRNA has been confirmed to be involved in the processes such as insulin biogenesis and secretion, programmed apoptosis of islet β cell, insulin resistance and islet inflammation, and was expected to be biomarker and therapeutic target of diabetes. The role of circRNA in the pathogenesis, diagnosis and treatment of different types of diabetes were systematically summarized in this review, in order to further understand the pathogenesis of diabetes and provide some ideas to find therapeutic approaches. © 2022, Editorial Board of Pharmaceutical Biotechnology. All right reserved.
