TI  - Phytochemicals as Drug Leads
PY  - 2022
T2  - Phytochemicals as Drug Leads
SP  - 1
EP  - 119
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85201639575&partnerID=40&md5=732d29ed2908c24397f78a6d4add910c
AB  - Functional bioactive compounds of plant origin have been an invaluable source for many human therapeutic drugs and have played a major role in the treatment of diseases around the world. These compounds possess enormous structural and chemical diversity and have led to many important discoveries. This communication, and accompanying lecture, highlights some of the authors continued efforts in anti-inflammatory drug discovery research, with a focus on the discovery of bioactive phytochemicals and an understanding of their mode of action. The author attempts to provide a brief understanding of the field of drug discovery science followed by a review of cellular and molecular mechanisms that regulate a variety of chronic inflammatory diseases. A brief review of phytochemicals that demonstrate great therapeutic potential follows after which three compounds, namely cardamonin, 2,6-bis(4- Hydroxy-3-Methoxybenzylidene) cyclohexanone (BHMC) and 2,4,6-Trihydroxy-3-geranyl acetophenone (tHGA), are introduced. These compounds are among the many compounds that the author has worked with throughout his 27 years in UPM. The material presented is selected from a much larger pool of research output so as to adhere to a theme and provide the reader clear flow of progression. Therefore, the contents of this communication is not an exhaustive documentation of every research project over the authors career, but rather a compilation of interesting findings with potential for further work. © University of Malayasia 2022. All rights reserved.
