VL  - 23
IS  - 8
C7  - e13453
DO  - 10.1111/obr.13453
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85127373842&doi=10.1111%2fobr.13453&partnerID=40&md5=90a0fe14e43119cd99baefc2c0e20917
AB  - Several studies bring strong evidence for an active role of vitamin D and its metabolites in physiological adipocyte and adipose tissue processes in adulthood. This role includes effects of vitamin D on key adipose tissue and adipocyte biology parameters, including adipogenesis, energy metabolism, and inflammation. Interestingly, recent data also point to a role of maternal vitamin D deficiency in adipocyte and adipose tissue metabolic programming in offspring. This review summarizes the current state of knowledge on the biological effect of vitamin D on adipocyte/adipose tissue physiology. © 2022 World Obesity Federation.
