TI  - Effect of metformin on liver vitamin B12 in high-fat diet-induced obese mice and relationship between vitamin B12 and glucose and lipid metabolism
ST  - 二甲双胍对高脂饮食诱导的肥胖小鼠肝脏维生素 B12 的影响及维生素 B12 与糖脂代谢的关系
PY  - 2022
T2  - Chinese Journal of Pathophysiology
VL  - 38
IS  - 7
SP  - 1226
EP  - 1233
DO  - 10.3969/j.issn.1000-4718.2022.07.010
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85168134038&doi=10.3969%2fj.issn.1000-4718.2022.07.010&partnerID=40&md5=c8706edfedff5a2e0c6cb1ca47cf9f24
AB  - AIM: To investigate whether metformin （Met） affects serum and liver vitamin B12 levels in C57BL/6J mice fed with high-fat diet （HFD）， and the correlation between vitamin B12 level and metabolic phenotypes. METHODS: Male C57BL/6J mice aged 7 to 8 weeks were fed with HFD for 12 weeks to establish an obese mouse model，and mice fed with chow diet （CD） were used as control group. The mice in each group were further divided into 2 groups: those in one group drunk water with Met at a dose of 250 mg·kg−1·d−1 for 4 weeks，and those in the other group drunk normal water as control. Namely the mice were randomly divided into 4 groups: CD group，CD Met group，HFD group and HFD Met group，with 5 mice in each group. During the dietary intervention，body weight and fasting blood glucose were measured. At the end of intervention，the mice were sacrificed and tissues were collected. Triglyceride （TG），total cholesterol （TC） and vitamin B12 levels in serum and liver were measured. Liver HE and oil red O staining were conducted. RESULTS: （1） Compared with CD group，body weight，and serum and liver lipid profiles in HFD group increased significantly，and liver histological observation results showed that lipid deposition was aggravated. （2） Compared with HFD group，body weight，liver TG and liver TC decreased significantly in HFD Met group，and liver histological observation results showed that lipid deposition was alleviated. （3） There was no significant difference in serum vitamin B12 levels among the 4 groups，but liver vitamin B12 levels showed significant reduction in HFD Met group compared with CD Met group （P<0.01）. （4） No correlation was observed between the serum vitamin B12 level and metabolic phenotypes. However，liver vitamin B12 level was negatively correlated with body weight，fasting blood glucose，liver weight，serum lipid levels，visceral adipose tissue weight and subcutaneous adipose tissue weight （P<0.05）. CONCLUSION: Metformin down-regulates vitamin B12 level in liver rather than in serum when treating the HFD-induced obese mice. The vitamin B12 level in liver was negatively correlated with body weight，liver weight，serum lipid profile and fasting blood glucose during the metformin treatment. © 2022 Chinese Journal of Pathophysiology. All rights reserved.
