AB  - A balanced diet during pregnancy is essential for maternal and fetal health. Maternal organs and systems undergo specific adaptations to support pregnancy and the gut microbiota does not seem to be an exception. It may play relevant roles in maternal metabolism and in the outcome of food-related hazards. In addition, the alteration of the gut microbiome may be related with negative pregnancy outcomes. Gut microbiota modulation during pregnancy, through the diet or the use of probiotics, prebiotics and related strategies, is an attractive target since it has the potential to impact on both women and infant health. © 2022 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
