AB  - Dietary supplementation can modulate the gut microbiota leading to positive effects on host health. This article outlines the most commonly used approaches: prebiotics, probiotics, synbiotics and micronutrients. Each section describes the different types of interventions, how they modulate the gut microbiota and scientific evidence on how supplementation affects certain disorders and/or diseases. © 2022 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
