TI  - Metformin inhibits ferroptosis via Nrf2-Gpx4 signaling pathway and minimizes liver damage in rats with non-alcoholic fatty liver disease
ST  - 二甲双胍经 Nrf2-Gpx4 通路抑制铁死亡并减轻非酒精性脂肪性肝病大鼠的肝损伤
PY  - 2021
T2  - Chinese Journal of Pathophysiology
VL  - 37
IS  - 10
SP  - 1848
EP  - 1857
DO  - 10.3969/j.issn.1000-4718.2021.10.015
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85168110932&doi=10.3969%2fj.issn.1000-4718.2021.10.015&partnerID=40&md5=c740828a48a23600106c66f1c8a9ecc8
AB  - AIM：To explore the effect of metformin（Met）on hepatic injury in non-alcoholic fatty liver disease（NAFLD）rats and the molecular mechanism based on nuclear factor E2-related factor 2（Nrf2）-glutathione peroxidase 4（Gpx4）-mediated ferroptosis signaling pathway. METHODS：SPF male SD rats were fed with high-fat diet to establish NAFLD model，and the rats in control group were fed with normal diet. After 12 weeks of feeding，the model rats were randomly divided into NAFLD group，Met low-dose（Met-L）group，Met high-dose（Met-H）group，and Met+brusatol （Nrf2 inhibitor）group，with 8 rats in each group. The rats in Met-L group and Met-H group were given 100 and 200 mg/kg Met by gavage，once daily. The rats in Met+brusatol group were given 200 mg/kg Met intragastrically and 2 mg/kg brusatol intraperitoneally every other day. The rats in control group and NAFLD group were given the same amount of normal saline intragastrically and intraperitoneally respectively，for 6 weeks. After the administration，the serum levels of aspartate aminotransferase（AST），alanine aminotransferase（ALT），total cholesterol（TC），triglycerides（TG），low-density lipoprotein cholesterol（LDL-C），high-density lipoprotein cholesterol（HDL-C），and inflammatory factors tumor necrosis factorα（TNF-α）and interleukin-6（IL-6）were detected. The ferri ion content in liver tissue homogenate was measured with colorimetric method，the malondialdehyde（MDA）content was detected with TBA method，the glutathione（GSH）content was detected with micro-enzyme method，the reactive oxygen species（ROS）content was detected with DCFH-DA fluorescent probe method. The pathological changes of liver tissue were observed with HE staining. The lipid accumulation in hepatic cells was determined by oil red O staining. The ferri deposition in the liver was examined with Prussian blue staining. The expression of Nrf2，heme oxygenase-1（HO-1），Gpx4 and cystine/glutamate antiporter（xCT）at protein and mRNA levels in the liver tissues was determined by Western blot and RT-qPCR，respectively. RESULTS：Compared with control group，the serum levels of ALT，AST，TNF-α，IL-6，TC，TG and LDL-C，liver ferri ion content，MDA，ROS levels，liver tissue NAS score，the percentage of oil red O staining and Prussian blue staining positive areas were significantly increased in NAFLD group（P<0. 05），the serum HDL-C level，liver tissue GSH content，Nrf2，HO-1，Gpx4，and xCT protein and mRNA expression were significantly reduced（P<0. 05），hepatocytes were arranged disorderly and swelling，lipid droplet vacuoles were presented in the cells，and there were obvious inflammatory cell infiltration，lipid accumulation and ferri deposition. Compared with NAFLD group，the serum levels of ALT，AST，TNF-α，IL-6，TC，TG and LDL-C，liver ferri ion content，MDA，ROS levels，liver tissue NAS score，the percentage of oil red O staining and Prussian blue staining positive areas were significantly reduced in Met-L group and Met-H group（P<0. 05），the serum HDL-C level，liver tissue GSH content，Nrf2，HO-1，Gpx4，and xCT protein and mRNA expression were significantly increased（P<0. 05），the fatty degeneration of liver cells was reduced，inflammatory cell infiltration，lipid accumulation and ferri deposition were reduced. And the Nrf2 inhibitor brusatol obviously reversed the activation effect of Met on the Nrf2/Gpx4 signaling pathway and its protective effect on liver of NAFLD rats. CONCLUSION：Met may activate the Nrf2/Gpx4 signaling pathway，inhibit ferroptosis，reduce the degree of lipid peroxidation，to exert a protective effect on liver of NAFLD rats. © 2022 Chinese Journal of Pathophysiology. All rights reserved.
