AB  - Background and aim: Objectives are to explore recent advances in discovery of new antidiabetic agents using repurposing strategies and to discuss modern technologies used for drug repurposing highlighting diabetic specific web portal. Methods: Recent literature were studied and analyzed from various sources such as Scopus, PubMed, and IEEE Xplore databases. Results: Drugs like Niclosamideethanolamine, Methazolamide, Diacerein, Berberine, Clobetasol, etc. with possibility of repurposing to curb diabetes can be potential late-stage clinical candidates, providing access to information on pharmacology, formulation, and probable toxicity if any. Conclusions: With collaboration of artificial intelligence (AI) with pharmacology, the efficiency of drug repurposing can improve significantly. © 2021 Diabetes India
