AB  - Hepatitis B,Hepatitis C,ami type 2 diabetes niellitus (T2DM) are serious public health issues worldwide.This article analyzes the association of Hepatitis B and Hepatitis C with T2DM.The analysts shows that on the one hand,both Hepatitis B and Hepatitis C promote the pathogenesis ofT2DM,which involves viral infection inhibiting insulin signal transduction as well as glucose uptake and glycogen synthe¬sis in insulin target cells; on the other hand,patients with T2D.M are prone to Hepatitis B and Hepatitis C,which may be associated with mul¬tiple organ dysfunction eaused by dial»etes. © 2021 Editorial Board of Jilin University. All Rights Reserved.
