UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85129822118&doi=10.1016%2fB978-0-323-89779-2.00009-0&partnerID=40&md5=ddd1a65d4f348253652749da2399beb3
AB  - Lycopene is one of the important members of the carotenoid family which is structurally a tetraterpene of eight isoprene units found abundantly in tomato and its derivative products. Lycopene is a non-pro-vitamin A carotenoid associated with high antioxidant activity. It has also been demonstrated to have wide variety of beneficial effects in the prevention and treatment of various diseases like diabetes mellitus, cardiovascular diseases, cancers, skin and bone ailments, neurological disorders, etc. In this chapter we have summarized the knowledge about this miracle compound, its structure, function, biochemical role, and possible mechanisms whereby it serves as miracle nutrient against various diseases. © 2022 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
