AB  - Although attention for fetal complications of multifetal pregnancies prevails in modern obstetric teaching and literature, it is a moral and medical imperative to also consider the health of the woman herself in clinical decision-making. Multifetal pregnancy poses her at increased risk of antepartum and peripartum complications compared to singleton pregnancies. It is important to be aware of such risks, and to, as much as possible, avoid iatrogenic multifetal pregnancies as well as medical procedures without medical indication, both of which may be harmful to the woman. © Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2021. All rights are reserved.
