AB  - Sirtuins are important regulators of multiple biological processes under normal or diseased conditions. Exosomes as extracellular vesicles with a size range of ~30-150nm in diameter emerge as essential messengers for intercellular communication and play diversified roles in normal physiology and in acquired abnormalities. At present, not much is known about the connections between Sirtuins and exosomes. In this review, we attempt to survey the current literature, summarizing the known factors that could link these two crucial entities in biology, and propose Sirtuins to be regulators and the regulated molecules of exosomes. © 2021 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
