UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85092140718&doi=10.1016%2fj.mmm.2020.07.007&partnerID=40&md5=2662c3860a72f393ce57d4d506756a4c
AB  - Many studies have shown that the dairy products consumption (milk, cheese, and fermented dairy products) is associated to a lower cardio-metabolic risk. They decrease weight gain, type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, and metabolic syndrome risk. Their consumption is linked to a lesser myocardial infarction, ischemic heart disease and cerebrovascular risk. Besides the role of calcium, many other components are able to play a role, explaining the matrix effect. Yogurt and other fermented dairy products are particularly involved in this beneficial effect. © 2020 Elsevier Masson SAS
