TI  - The role of diosgenin in diabetes and diabetic complications
PY  - 2020
T2  - Journal of Steroid Biochemistry and Molecular Biology
VL  - 198
C7  - 105575
DO  - 10.1016/j.jsbmb.2019.105575
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85078184319&doi=10.1016%2fj.jsbmb.2019.105575&partnerID=40&md5=15a853e5d5b8d91f5b6b0730438a333e
AB  - Diabetes mellitus is a chronic and common metabolic disease that seriously endangers human health. Hyperglycemia and long-term metabolic disorders in diabetes will cause damage to the whole body tissues and organs, resulting in serious complications. Nowadays, drugs for treating diabetes on the market has strong side effects, new treatments thus are urgently needed. Natural therapy of natural ingredients is a promising avenue, this is because natural ingredients are safer and they also show strong activity in the treatment of diabetes. Diosgenin is such a very biologically active natural steroidal sapogenin. The research of diosgenin in the treatment of diabetes and its complications has been widely reported. This article reviews the effects of diosgenin through multiple targets and multiple pathways in diabetes and its complications which including diabetic nephropathy, diabetic liver disease, diabetic neuropathy, diabetic vascular disease, diabetic cardiomyopathy, diabetic reproductive dysfunction, and diabetic eye disease. © 2019 Elsevier Ltd
