AB  - Macrophages are one of the most important innate immune cells in human, which have high heterogeneity and plasticity. According to different micro-environmental stimuli conditions, macrophage polarization can be divided into Ml and M2 subsets. The M1/M2 phenotype of macrophages is related to the pathological process of various diseases, but the molecular mechanisms have not yet been elucidated. This article reviews macrophage polarization and the related diseases, such as tumors, metabolic diseases, inflammatory diseases, highlights the important role of M1/M2 balance, and provides a new target and direction for clinical treatment. © 2020 Publication Centre of Anhui Medical University. All rights reserved.
