AB  - Pregnancy regulates immune system and inflammatory processes. Low grade inflammation is responsible for the development of gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM). The process begins in first trimester and both T and B lymphocytes play role. Inflammation of the adipose tissue and liver is critical for the development of GDM. Obesity and excess weight gain contribute to development of inflammation. © 2020 by Nova Science Publishers, Inc. All rights reserved.
