TI  - Effect of Puerarin in Reducing Insulin Resistance in HepG2 Cells via PI3K/Akt/GSK-3j8 Signal Transduction Pathway
ST  - 葛根素通过 PI3K/Akt/GSK-3/3 信号通路调节 HepG2 细胞胰岛素抵抗
PY  - 2019
T2  - Chinese Journal of Experimental Traditional Medical Formulae
VL  - 25
IS  - 12
SP  - 77
EP  - 82
DO  - 10.13422/j.cnki.syfjx.20191204
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85173918548&doi=10.13422%2fj.cnki.syfjx.20191204&partnerID=40&md5=74039c9c6eaf8b0caf9ee7d83e10975d
AB  - Objective : To observe the effect of puerarin on phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase (PI3K), protein kinase B (Akt) and glycogen synthase kinase-3^S (GSK-3/3) in insulin resistant HepG2 cells. Method : HepG2 cells were treated with palmitic acid 0. 5 mmol'L ~ and insulin 9x10 U *L ~ to induce insulin resistant condition for 24 h. Cell viability was detected by methyl thiazolyl tetrazolium (MTT) assay to determine the concentration of puerarin. This experiment included normal control group, model control group and puerarin groups of different doses (40, 80, 160, 320 (xg*L) - Glucose detection kit was used to detect the content of glucose in cell culture supernatant. Tumor necrosis factor alpha (TNF-a) and interleukin-6 (IL-6) levels in supernatant of cell culture medium were detected by enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) - Hepatic glycogen assay kit was used for detecting the hepatic glycogen content in HepG2 cells. Western blot was applied to detect protein expression levels of PI3K, Akt, pAkt, GSK-3jS and p-GSK-3^S. Result ； Compared with those in the normal control group, the glucose consumption rate was significantly down-regulated in HepG2 cells in the model control group (P < 0. 05), the intracellular glycogen content was decreased (P < 0. 05), the content of TNF-a and IL-6 were increased in supernatant of cell culture medium (P < 0. 05), PI3K protein level was decreased, Akt phosphorylation level was down-regulated (P < 0. 05), and GSK-3/3 protein expression was up-regulated (P < 0. 05). Compared with those in the model control group, in the puerarin groups, the glucose consumption rate was increased in a dose-dependent manner (P < 0. 05), the intracellular glycogen content was increased, the contents of TNF-ct and IL-6 were reduced in supernatant of cell culture medium (P < 0. 05), PI3K protein expression was enhanced, Akt phosphorylation level was up-regulated (P < 0. 05), GSK-3yS protein expression was down-regulated, but its phosphorylation inactivation was increased (P < 0. 05). Conclusion : Puerarin alleviates the insulin resistance of HepG2 cells by strengthening the PI3 K/Akt/GSK-3jS signal transduction process and increasing the glycogen content in hepatocytes. © 2019 Chinese Journal of Experimental Traditional Medical Formulae. All rights reserved.
