AB  - Soy is a biologically active plant composed of protein and several bioactive components such as genistein, daidzein, and aglycin. Evidence from both animal and human studies supports soy protein or its bioactive components having a favorable effect on glucoregulation, insulin resistance, body weight, and fat mass, which are hallmarks of diabetes mellitus. Potential mechanisms whereby soy protein and bioactive components may exert preventive and/or therapeutic effects are discussed, including a wide spectrum of biochemical and molecular activities. The potential of soybean flour for the recovery of nutritional status after protein restriction during intrauterine life and lactation is also covered. © 2019 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
