AB  - The purpose of the chapter is to view the global burden of diabetes and its preventive strategies, especially in high-risk groups. According to the IDF Diabetes Atlas 8th edition of the International Diabetes Federation, currently 425million people live with diabetes and this number is predicted to rise to 629million by 2045. Asian countries, especially China and India, are witnessing mounting epidemics of prediabetes and diabetes. The dramatic rise in new onset diabetes has been attributed to the rapid transition of demographic, socioeconomic, and nutritional factors. The change in dietary patterns coupled with a sedentary lifestyle has led to obesity and diabetes. Therefore the growing burden of diabetes should be prevented or treated with great importance. Lifestyle intervention with proper diet and physical activity has already proven its efficacy in the prevention and treatment of diabetes. However, there are several limitations existing in the present therapeutic approaches to the prevention and treatment of diabetes, and these should be addressed through novel strategies. The chapter focuses on the present understanding of the contributing factors, preventive strategies, and scope and challenges of diabetes prevention and treatment. © 2018 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
