AB  - Severe obesity as a serious public health concern requires efficacious treatment. Sedentary behavior is associated with a lot of metabolic and cardiovascular comorbidities like diabetes, metabolic syndrome, and cardiovascular disease. Term “life style” includes dietary habits and physical activity. Life style interventions, as a first step in obesity treatment can help severely obese individuals to achieve long-term weight loss. The aim of life style modifications is to reduce the burden of obesity and obesity related comorbidities. Dietary treatment is probably the first and main therapeutic approach to obesity. This treatment is based on negative energy balance caused by lower energy intake but also in change in composition of food and proper rhythm of meals. Diets have to be medically confirmed and patient tailored. Increased physical activity is very important for weight loss maintaining. Self-monitoring or group support could be very useful in maintained the intense of physical activity over a long period of time. Current recommendations are that adults should have at least 150 min of moderate-intensity physical activity during a week. Conscious cognitive processes play important role in weight reduction and maintaining weight. Specific cognitive factors are associated with unhealthy eating habits, dietary treatment discontinuation and weight loss maintenance. © 2019 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
