TI  - The Potential of Epigenetic Compounds in Treating Diabetes
PY  - 2018
T2  - Epigenetics in Human Disease
SP  - 489
EP  - 547
DO  - 10.1016/B978-0-12-812215-0.00017-0
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85125543641&doi=10.1016%2fB978-0-12-812215-0.00017-0&partnerID=40&md5=2733cc3654f061dd08461b8111febcc7
AB  - Globally, diabetes (and in particular type 2 diabetes) continues to present as a major health challenge worldwide. Despite our efforts, our understanding of the genetic events underpinning diabetes pathogenesis remains poor. Altered epigenetics has, however, been firmly associated with many aspects critical to diabetes pathogenesis, and our increased understanding in this area has resulted in the identification of several therapeutic options with potential for the management of diabetes. This chapter outlines how epigenetics is altered in diabetes, how this may contribute to diabetes pathogenesis, and summarizes how targeting epigenetics may have significant potential benefit in the treatment of this condition. © 2018 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
