AB  - Type 2 diabetes is caused by complex interactions between genetic and environmental factors. Comprehensive metabolite profiling or "metabolomics" defines the chemical phenotype of biological systems and explores their integrated responses to genetic variation and environmental changes. Thus, application of metabolomics in childhood obesity can play a key role in defining novel disease mechanisms and targets for early diabetes prevention and treatment. This chapter seeks to review the application of metabolomics to childhood obesity, insulin resistance, and type 2 diabetes. © Springer International Publishing AG 2018.
