AB  - Metabolomics, or the comprehensive profiling of small molecule metabolites in cells, tissues, or whole organisms, has undergone a rapid technological evolution in the past two decades. These advances have led to the application of metabolomics to defining predictive biomarkers for incident cardiometabolic diseases and, increasingly, as a blueprint for understanding those diseases’ pathophysiologic mechanisms. Progress in this area and challenges for the future are reviewed here. © 2017 Elsevier Inc.
