TI  - Smoking and the risk of type 2 diabetes
PY  - 2017
T2  - Translational Research
VL  - 184
SP  - 101
EP  - 107
DO  - 10.1016/j.trsl.2017.02.004
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85017127276&doi=10.1016%2fj.trsl.2017.02.004&partnerID=40&md5=139e93e5b094ff3e9e675ec2e1461bda
AB  - Despite accumulating evidence demonstrating strong epidemiologic and mechanistic associations between cigarette smoking, hyperglycemia, and the development of type 2 diabetes, tobacco abuse has not been uniformly recognized as a modifiable risk factor in diabetes prevention or screening strategies. In this review, we highlight population-based studies that have linked cigarette smoking with an increased risk of type 2 diabetes and summarize clinical and preclinical studies offering insight into mechanisms through which cigarette smoking and nicotine exposure impact body composition, insulin sensitivity, and pancreatic β cell function. Key questions for future studies are identified and strategies for smoking cessation as a means to decrease diabetes risk are discussed. © 2017 Elsevier Inc.
