AB  - Metabolic syndrome predisposes to diabetes mellitus and cardiovascular disease, being an important issue for public health. A sufficient number of studies indicate that Taurine has a beneficial role against metabolic syndrome establishment by lowering oxidation of lipids, improving insulin resistance, regulating renin-angiotensin network, and lowering arterial pressure. This review summarizes the in vitro and in vivo research findings of beneficial abilities of taurine in obesity, dislipidemia, and diabetes mellitus. Also an investigation of possible molecular pathways of preventing metabolic syndrome with the use of taurine is included.
