AB  - Besides hepatic manifestations of hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection, some extrahepatic systemic and/or autoimmune manifestations may occur with both acute and chronic viral infections, usually independent of hepatic involvement. The most common one is the prodromal preicteric flu-like syndrome with arthralgias and sometimes urticarial cutaneous rash, observed in some patients with acute infection. Other extrahepatic manifestations include HBV-related glomerulonephritis or HBV-associated vasculitis (mainly polyarteritis nodosa type). © 2017 Elsevier B.V.
