DO  - 10.5603/AH.2016.0004
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84976905672&doi=10.5603%2fAH.2016.0004&partnerID=40&md5=81c7a28b67127311f6f5f8881dbb5802
AB  - Irisin is a myokine secreted by skeletal muscles. It has been proposed to drive the brown-fat-like conversion of the white adipose tissue. By enhancing energy expenditure, irisin may affect systemic metabolism and be associated with insulin resistance; however, the mechanism(s) of action still remain largely unexplained. The discovery of irisin can contribute to the exploration of the novel and effective therapeutic targets or therapeutic strategies of metabolic diseases or metabolism-associated health issues. In this review, based on the recent literature (from 2013 to 2015 inclusive), we will systematically discuss the associations of irisin with obesity, type 2 diabetes, lipid disorders, and hypertension. We also introduce unanswered questions for future research. © 2016 Via Medica.
