AB  - Diabetes is characterized by increased blood glucose. Its onset is attributable to both genetic and environmental factors. Dietary lipid intake in excess is one of the risk factors of type 2 diabetes. This chapter reviews the effects of total dietary lipid and lipid classes on insulin sensitivity and diabetes risk. The molecular mechanisms involved in the onset and progression of diabetes in adipose tissue, liver, muscle, and pancreatic β-cells are described. © 2016 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
