TI  - The protective functions of omentin in cardiovascular diseases
PY  - 2015
T2  - Clinica Chimica Acta
VL  - 448
SP  - 98
EP  - 106
DO  - 10.1016/j.cca.2015.05.019
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84934757615&doi=10.1016%2fj.cca.2015.05.019&partnerID=40&md5=3b9910f1107467c345b29875afa6ca7a
AB  - Adipose tissue is considered as a large gland that can produce paracrine and endocrine hormones. Growing evidence suggests that adipocytes may link obesity to cardiovascular diseases (CVD). Adipose tissue produces a large number of mediators, which affect metabolism, inflammation and coagulation. Omentin, a novel adipocytokine, has come into the center of interest due to its favorable effects on inflammation, glucose homeostasis and CVD. The present review provides a concise and general overview on the roles of omentin in CVD. The knowledge of these concepts may provide a new strategy to reduce disease risks on CVD in the future. © 2015 Elsevier B.V.
