AB  - Obesity may be secondary to other diseases due to genetic or acquired conditions that are characterized by alterations in the control of systems regulating hunger-satiety and / or weight, in the gastrointestinal system and the intestinal microbiota, in endocrine pathways. Secondary obesity may be due to maternal metabolic conditions, to neurobiological and psychological determinants, to sleep debt and smoking cessation, to disability and to various medications. © 2015 by Nova Science Publishers, Inc. All rights reserved.
