AB  - The modulation of microbiota could have favourable effects on weight and/or the inflammatory component of obesity. The results of studies on probiotics carried out on humans are not unequivocal, due to the heterogeneity of the populations studied and a strain-dependent effect. Other studies need to be carried out, notably involving pregnant women. The data concerning prebiotics, fewer in number, reveal favourable biological effects, notably on low-grade inflammation. Finally, some studies have been carried out on symbiotics, a mix of pro- and prebiotics. © 2015 Elsevier Masson SAS.
