AB  - Metabolic syndrome comprises a group of correlated clinical features which have insulin resistance (IR) as a common pathogenic determinant. It can lead to type 2 diabetes mellitus, nonalcoholic fatty liver disease and cardiovascular disorders. Some studies have shown that metabolic syndrome is a risk factor for hepatic tissue injure in patients with chronic viral hepatitis, but the conclusion is still a controversial issue. This article reviewed the advances in study on metabolic syndrome and viral hepatitis.
