UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84875400818&doi=10.1016%2fj.annfar.2012.12.008&partnerID=40&md5=7eda474647c22c3ed7b724bd58479465
AB  - Gestational diabetes insipidus is an uncommon clinical disease whose prevalence is approximately two to three pregnancies per 100,000. It may be isolated or associated with preeclampsia. We report a case of gestational diabetes insipidus in a twin pregnancy, originally isolated during two months, and secondarily complicated by HELLP-syndrome. We recall the specific pathophysiology of polyuric-polydipsic syndrome during pregnancy and summarize its various causes. Finally, we discuss the indications, in case of isolated gestational diabetes insipidus, of treatment by dDAVP. © 2013 .
