AB  - Adipokines are important metabolically effective hormones produced by adipose tissue. The research and clinical findings published within the last ten years clearly suggest that obesity-related wrongly regulated production of these mediators can contribute to the pathogenesis of the different phenotypes of the metabolic syndrome, such as dyslipidemia, insulin resistance, type 2 diabetes mellitus, inflammation, and atherosclerosis. Adiponectin is one of the few beneficial factors influencing metabolism and vascular properties. In obese subjects the level of adiponectin secreted by adipose tissue is reduced. This paper presents a survey of the molecular and clinical properties of this adipokine.
