AB  - There are many complications of multiple gestations. Preterm labor is the most common complication, and its definitive treatment has not been established. In addition to preterm labor, preeclampsia, gestational hypertension, PPROM, and anemia are significant problems encountered frequently in multiple gestations. The number of complications can be reduced by early and regular prenatal care by a staff familiar with these challenges. © 2005 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
